  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Identifying Dependencies**\n\nI\'m currently identifying the core dependencies for this project. The list includes `lucide-react`, `motion` (imported correctly), and standard React dependencies like `react`, `react-dom`, and `vite`. It\'s a purely front-end project; no backend integration dependencies are needed, like firebase. This landing page is going to be visually and functionally complete.\n\n\n**Defining Client-Side Logic**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the client-side specifics for this project. No mock databases are needed. This is where I\'m focusing on defining the interactive elements. I\'m adding a pain assessment tool, styled for elegant user interactions, and a breathing regulator exercise. These will be visually enriched using custom gold animations against the black background.\n\n\n**Adding Interactive Features**\n\nI\'m expanding the interactive elements to create more user engagement. I\'m adding an FAQ section explaining TCC, an interactive cost/agenda calculator for personalized summaries, and patient testimonials with animations. Lastly, I\'m composing a detailed profile about Dr. Bruno de Oliveira Lima, highlighting his expertise and approach. I\'ll need to review the global CSS and font selection.\n\n\n**Prioritizing Typography Choices**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on typography. I think the fonts are the most critical part of the design, and I want them to convey the right vibe. For an elegant look, I plan on using \"Playfair Display\" for headings and \"Inter\" for copy or \"Space Grotesk.\" I\'ve just added the import statements for \"Playfair Display\" and \"Inter\" from Google Fonts into the CSS file. I am looking at how to include the `@theme` definition for Tailwind CSS v4, which will automatically import the custom properties into the tailwind config.\n\n\n**Defining Color Palette**\n\nI\'m now focusing on color and component modularity. I\'ve been considering Tailwind V4\'s color customization options. I\'m exploring defining a luxurious color palette, including gold shades and deep grays, directly in the `index.css` or using Tailwind\'s theme mapping. I\'ve also planned modular components and type definitions for better project structure. I\'m going to create `types.ts` for all types and components such as `Navigation` in `/src/components/Navigation`.\n\n\n**Structuring Component Hierarchy**\n\nI\'m now outlining the component structure for the project. I\'m focusing on creating modular, reusable components for a consistent user experience. I\'ve got `/src/components/Navigation.tsx` for the elegant floating navigation. Also, I am planning for the hero section with `/src/components/Hero.tsx`. I\'ve outlined the approach, pain points, breathing exercise, self-assessment, appointment planner, testimonials and footer components.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 8
      nanos: 170692740
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
