urrent file system structure.\n\n\n**Clarifying File Access**\n\nI\'m now backpedaling on the `/public` directory issue. It\'s becoming clear that the core question is *where* the user-uploaded files are accessible from within the Google AI Studio Build environment. My suspicion is that, since `/public` doesn\'t exist, Vite might not be directly serving them from a standard filesystem path. I\'m focusing on how the platform might inject or handle these files differently. I\'m revisiting my search, wondering if a system folder holds the key, and I will be looking at the output from our `deepSearch` script.\n\n\n**Pinpointing File Origin**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the precise origin of user-uploaded files. The directory scan results are in, and `/workspace` and `/www-data-home` are empty, meaning files like `input_file_0.png` aren\'t present on disk within the container. I see that the scan *did* explore `/app/applet`, but the results did not include these files. This strongly suggests the files aren\'t stored locally. I\'m now hypothesizing that the files might exist only in the chat\'s frontend environment, and not accessible through the filesystem directly. I will be looking for an environment variable or URL that may contain a path to the files.\n\n\n**Uncovering Image Serving**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on why images are broken in the live preview. The user\'s report confirms that images like `/input_file_0.png` are not loading within the preview, pointing to a discrepancy with the server configuration. The crucial insight is that requests for these images are being directed to the Vite development server within the container, which lacks a `/public` directory. I\'m now focused on how the platform exposes user-uploaded files to the container environment, as they clearly aren\'t directly on the filesystem. I\'m searching for information on how the platform manages user uploads or input files.\n\n\n**Exploring System Skills**\n\nI\'m now shifting gears to scrutinize system skills, particularly in relation to image handling. Examining the available skills list, I\'ve re-evaluated the `image-generation` skill in the context of the file access issue. I\'ve considered that the input images might be stored differently than initially thought. I\'m also now running a script to perform a wide-ranging search of recent modifications. I\'m going to start exploring `/app` directly.\n\n\n**Investigating File Persistence**\n\nI\'m now pursuing a different angle, questioning the assumption of pre-existing files. I\'m checking if the system has files in the current or parent directory with alternate names. I\'m also now running a check on `/app/applet/public`, even though it seemed unlikely, and also `/app/applet/src` and `/app/applet/src/components` after that. I\'m also looking at the browser URL for any clues about Vite\'s file handling and whether the images need to be generated instead of being present. The `generate_image` tool could be the mechanism for creating those apparent files on-demand.\n\n\n"
